{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Link entities to one another, build trees of parents and children, and query entities by what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they’re linked to."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/RelatingEntities"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ChildOf","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AncestorsView","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/DescendantsView","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/CyclicHierarchy","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/HierarchyError"],"anchor":"Building-Hierarchies","title":"Building Hierarchies"}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some state belongs to a pair of entities rather than to one: a unit likes another, a turret aims"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at a ship, a button sits on a panel. A "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"relation","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" stores that kind of link, and the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"hierarchy","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the relation that makes trees of parents and children."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Link Entities with Relations","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Link-Entities-with-Relations"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare a relation as a type that conforms to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Relation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", then link a source entity to a target"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/relate(_:_:to:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and unlink it with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/unrelate(_:_:from:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Read the links in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"either direction: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/targets(_:of:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lists what a source relates to, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/sources(_:of:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lists what relates to a target."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A relation can carry values, one per link, such as the amount one entity owes another. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chooses two behaviors with static properties:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Relation\/isExclusive","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" limits a source to one target, so relating it to a new target","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replaces the old one.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Relation\/onTargetDespawn"},{"text":" says what despawning a target does to its sources: remove their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"links, the default, or despawn them too.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A source holds its links in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Targets","isActive":true},{"text":" component, which you read and filter on like any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component. To visit only the sources of one target, filter a query with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".related(_:to:)"},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uses the world’s index of each target’s sources rather than walking every source.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Build a Hierarchy","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Build-a-Hierarchy"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The hierarchy is the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ChildOf","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" relation: exclusive, so each entity has at most one parent, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"despawning a parent despawns its children, and theirs in turn. Spawn an entity under a parent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/spawn(_:childOf:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", or move an existing one with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/addChild(_:to:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/CyclicHierarchy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" rather than make an entity its own ancestor. Walk the tree with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/parent(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/children(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/ancestors(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/descendants(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because the hierarchy is a relation, the same query filters work on it:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".related(ChildOf.self, to: ship)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" visits the children of ","type":"text"},{"code":"ship","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".without(Targets<ChildOf>.self)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" visits the roots.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example aims a ship’s turret at a comet, then at a moon, and despawns the ship"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with its turret:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct AimsAt: Relation {","    static var isExclusive: Bool { true }","}","","var world = World()","let ship = world.spawn(Name(value: \"ship\"))","let turret = world.spawn(Name(value: \"turret\"), childOf: ship)","let comet = world.spawn(Name(value: \"comet\"))","let moon = world.spawn(Name(value: \"moon\"))","","world.relate(turret, AimsAt(), to: comet)","world.relate(turret, AimsAt(), to: moon)","print(world.targets(AimsAt.self, of: turret) == [moon])","\/\/ Prints \"true\"","","world.despawn(ship)","print(world.contains(turret), world.sources(AimsAt.self, of: moon).isEmpty)","\/\/ Prints \"false true\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Observers of an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityEvent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" that propagates also use the hierarchy: the event moves from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entity it was triggered on up to each of its ancestors. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" record changes to relations","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and to the hierarchy, to apply after a query or update.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Relating Entities","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"role":"article"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/relatingentities"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/sources(_:of:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/sources(_:of:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sources","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"R","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"R","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6EntityV","text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6EntityV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"sources(_:of:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/sources(_:of:)","abstract":[{"text":"Returns the entities that relate to a target by a relation, in the order they were","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"related.","type":"text"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/DescendantsView":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/descendantsview","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DescendantsView","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DescendantsView","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A lazy sequence of an entity’s descenda